
public class InheritanceConceptMain {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Multiple and Hybrid Inheritance");
        System.out.println("Java does not support multiple inheritance");
        System.out.println("of classes directly.");
        System.out.println("Interfaces can support multiple");
        System.out.println("inheritance of type.");
    }
}

/*
Multiple inheritance means a class inherits from
more than one parent class.

Java does not allow:
class C extends A, B

This avoids ambiguity when both parent classes
contain the same method.

Hybrid inheritance combines two or more forms
of inheritance.

Interfaces are commonly used when Java needs
multiple or hybrid inheritance of type/behavior.
No interface is implemented in this program.
*/
